   Teknologi Malaysia, Inst Sultan Iskandar},
Abstract = {This study proposes to build a framework that can able to explain the
   behavior of the consumer towards changing their consumption pattern
   toward using organic product. In Malaysia, the growth rate of the
   consumer adoption towards organic consumption is slow for the past ten
   years. This study focuses on the Malaysian consumer valued organic
   product and how their own personal value affects them in buying organic
   product. The study start on reviewing past literature on organic and
   consumer behavior related to their attitude toward food and organic
   product. Perceived value of the consumer and their personal values has
   been highlighted as among of the factors that is important to consumer
   when they make decision making to purchase product. The theory of
   planned behavior is used as the basis of this framework because many
   past researchers still regard this theory as one of the important theory
   in explaining the consumer behavior. This study expects to get the
   insight of the predicting factor that is important in building the
   positive consumers' attitude toward organic product. This study enable
   to suggest to the manufacturer on how to improve the marketing
   strategies in order to increase the intention of purchasing of organic
   product.},
